+# UD Nonlinear orbital instability v0.1
+
+Conditional theorem under the existing joint Hamiltonian. No action term, species or coefficient has been changed. Constructor review only; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.
+
+Read the eleven-page PDF. It supplies a conserved co-moving Gram matrix, an exact force-canceling sector, nonlinear Coulomb equations, a self-contained finite-Fourier comparison lemma, fixed-norm admissible seeds and a gauge-invariant orbital-departure proof. Four resonances and zero stiffness have separate constructions. Six positive parameter values remain explicitly OPEN.
+
+Replay: `python3 verify_nonlinear_orbital.py` with Python 3, SymPy, NumPy and SciPy. The graph module is a preserved copy of the preceding mode release's `mode_model.py`. Exact algebra checks and numerical nonlinear campaigns produce separate receipts. The verifier is not an independent proof review or a machine verification of an averaging theorem.
+
+Build PDF: run `pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error UD_NONLINEAR_ORBITAL_INSTABILITY_v0.1.tex` twice.
+
+The older mode release remains frozen. Its nonlinear OPEN question is partially resolved here for the specified nonzero flat family, not for other backgrounds or the six remaining resonances. The prior positive-stiffness zero-matter vacuum stability and global flow completeness results are preserved.
+
+No experimental data were used. The missing image Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png was not used. This is a mathematical diagnostic for a candidate action, not a physical instability claim.
